  "security_implications": "The chunk directly controls the SHA engine start/continue/process signals and the hash_done routing based on hmac_en_i. If hmac_en_i is not strictly controlled or is toggled during operation, the core can be forced into raw SHA mode, exposing intermediate digests that may be correlated with the HMAC secret key. The OR combination of reg_hash_process_i and hash_process also creates a potential double-trigger path to the SHA engine, which could disrupt the HMAC sequence. Both constitute integrity and confidentiality risks that must be verified in the full design.",
